  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The reaction is:</p><p><math> <mrow> <mtext>P</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>Q</mtext> <mo>&#8594;</mo> <mtext>R</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>S</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>rate</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>the</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>reaction</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msup><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></msup></math><br />The concentration of Q varies with time as per the graph by the equation.<br /><math> <mrow> <mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>Q</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> <mo>=</mo> <mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>Q</mtext> <mn>0</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mfenced> <mo>-</mo> <mtext>kt &#8203;</mtext></mrow></math> i.e. Zero-order kinetics.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />With respect to reactant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math></p><p>let time taken for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></math> completion of the reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math>.</p><p>Then the time is taken for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>75</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp; complication will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></msub></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>75</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></msub></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>at</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><msub><mo>]</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><msub><mo>]</mo><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>75</mn><mo>%</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><msub><mo>]</mo><mrow><mn>75</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math><br />As we can see, in each time interval of &#39;a&#39; min the reactant concentration&nbsp;is changing by factor half. therefore rate constant is independent of the concentration of the reactant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math>. hence with respect of reactant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math>, order of the reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>.&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />Rate law expression is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>rate</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mfenced><mn>1</mn></msup><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mfenced><mn>0</mn></msup></math><br />The overall order of reaction&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>",
